{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/594641-what-changes-for-wraiths-when-if-they-can-cross-the-shroud","id":594641,"title":"what changes for wraiths when/if they can cross the Shroud?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T05:10:49-07:00","id":594641,"title":"what changes for wraiths when/if they can cross the Shroud?","content":"Since wraiths can see Skinlands from Shadowlands, what changes for wraiths when/if they can cross the Shroud? How do they perceive the world then? Would it mean anything for the living?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6954-beyefendikus","name":"Beyefendikus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:03:35-07:00","id":594864,"title":"","content":"Well thematically it changes a huge amount of the game and reduces the importance of the Tempest, Dark Kingdoms, and Labyrinth. It would make it much easier for Wraiths to protect their fetters and engage in their passions, which would probably have the effect of making their inevitable decline much less certain. Hauntings would become much more common, and likely not limited to specific places where the Shroud is low. Spectres probably wouldn't flood across the Shroud intentionally, since they have a hard time perceiving the Skinlands, but the every local Maelstrom would probably push some across. So things are going to get quite a bit darker in the world of the living.<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason why Wraiths still wouldn't see the world in terms of Deathsight and Lifesight, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:00:17-07:00","id":594901,"title":"","content":"Can you tell me whic book i can read more detailed information about tis toppic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6954-beyefendikus","name":"Beyefendikus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:33:37-07:00","id":594935,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Most of that is extrapolation from what's in the Core book. I'm not sure where it says Spectres have a harder time seeing across the Shroud, and upon checking out Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth (which is an excellent sourcebook) some Spectres do indeed tend to Fetters. So I guess some of them would cross on their own. A lot of Spectres, though, are oblivion eaten enough (or just spent too long trapped in the Labyrinth) that they lost their Fetters, and <i>they</i> would have a hard time even existing above the Tempest without a Maelstrom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T00:25:41-07:00","id":595457,"title":"","content":"Dark Reflections: Spectres says Spectres have a harder time seeing across the Shroud and influencing the Skinlands' inhabitants (page 17, sub-heading 'Distance'), reflected as a +2 difficulty to all Mental Trait rolls dealing with interaction with the mortal world. The previewed Spectre chapter for Wr20 reiterates this.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't see any Nephwracks tending to Fetters, since part of the Nephwrack definition is that they have no Fetters. Dark Reflections says only Doppelgangers and Mortwrights have Fetters; Wr20 lets Shades do so as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:47:16-07:00","id":595713,"title":"","content":"There's also the Risen... If they count. They've essentially crossed over. How about wraiths that have the Embody Arcanos?<br /> <br /> Also Doomslayers and Spectres can have 'Shroud-Rending' Arcanos, which is an arcanos specifically used to look through the Shroud, making it seem that Spectres really can only see the Shadowlands and not the Skinlands clearly without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T08:10:28-07:00","id":597006,"title":"","content":"For some reason I was under the impression that you were asking what would happen if you changed the game so that wraiths could pass the shroud more easily. Re reading I see that you weren't so I will check my books tonight to see if I can get you a better answer. Note: I don't have the guildbooks, but I do have Risen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:46:50-07:00","id":597110,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Spectres book describes spectres seeing the Shadowlands as an apocalyptic decayed landscape populated only by wraiths and themselves. I think they need to use Arcanoi to perceive living beings and structures in the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:26:25-07:00","id":598514,"title":"","content":"So Risen and manifested ghosts still have Lifesight and Deathsight and still need Pathos, so in broad strokes the Skinlands still look the same: full of energy and emotion but also of death and decay. I think its the incidentals that would mean the most: The feeling of sun on your skin, the light breeze, the touch of another living person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T16:57:29-07:00","id":598794,"title":"","content":"Does a Risen have a restored human sense of touch? Would one feel any warmth that did not burn? Any cold that does not freeze? Any touch that does not wound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T04:54:04-07:00","id":599207,"title":"","content":"I remember a description of a fully manifested Wraith having those sensations and being completely overwhelmed by the simple forgotten sensations. I think you are correct about Risen, their senses are dulled compared to a living person, but even those dulled senses are going to provide contexts and feelings a Wraith's Corpus just doesn't. It's not the same as living flesh, possibly even worse than nothing for some wraiths since it is so close and yet so far away, but it is a kind of sensation Wraiths usually don't get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:42:20-07:00","id":600007,"title":"","content":"Definitely worse than nothing; coming back Risen is all kinds of Angst for the Shadow in terms of sensations.<br /> <br /> Like -almost- being able to touch the one you love goes to being able to touch them... but its just not THE SAME. <i><b>.struh</b></i> <b><i>ylIaer ti teb I !esirprus eht liops ot tnaw t'ndid I </i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4221-mrvyngaard","name":"MrVyngaard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4221_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}